@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-09
@reviewed: 2026-10-15

Feature: Setup Command
  "CLI handler for mason setup <server>: run onboarding (setup.Run) with terminal confirmations and progress, and summarize what changed."

  Provides:
    - cli.newSetupCommand @source("symbol:newSetupCommand")
    - cli.defaultSetupRun @source("symbol:defaultSetupRun")

  Consumes:
    - setup.Run
    - setup.Params
    - cli.confirmPrompt

  Invariants:
    - setup MUST require exactly one server argument
    - Progress lines MUST go to stderr and be silenced by --quiet and --json
    - setup MUST NOT multiplex SSH connections, since it is testing which credentials work
    - --print MUST write only the scripts to stdout
    - The summary MUST say "Already set up" when nothing changed, and name the key and config paths

  OutOfScope:
    - Onboarding logic (setup.Run)

  Scenario (happy-path): Fresh machine
    Given setup.Run reports a generated key and a bootstrap
    When mason setup example.com runs
    Then stdout says "Set up", names the key and ~/.mason, and suggests mason init

  Scenario (negative): Missing server
    Given no argument
    When mason setup runs
    Then it fails before calling setup.Run
